    <p class="eyebrow">Practice guide</p>
    <h1>Advocacy in the Fair Work Commission</h1>
    <p class="lead">You may have to run a Commission hearing yourself. This guide explains how: the documents to file, how to prepare witnesses, where to sit, when to stand, and what to say at each stage. It uses unfair dismissal hearings as the model and includes sample wording you can adapt.</p>

    <div class="notice">
      <strong>Check current procedure first.</strong> Members run their hearings differently, and the Commission's directions for your matter override anything here. Read the directions, the relevant practice notes and the Commission's own <a href="https://www.fwc.gov.au/hearings-decisions/how-commission-works/prepare-conference-or-hearing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Prepare for a conference or hearing</a> guide. The conventions described on this page are common practice, not rules. The people, employer and events in the examples are fictional.
    </div>

